<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Bourbon Spain</h1><p class="st-meta">1700 CE – 1868 CE · capital Madrid</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Spain under the Bourbon dynasty from Philip V to Isabella II, a time of centralising reform, Napoleonic invasion and the loss of most of its American empire.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-of-spain">Charles II</a>, last of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/habsburg-spain">Habsburg Spain</a>, left the throne to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-v-of-spain">Philip of Anjou</a>, grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a>, who became Philip V in 1700. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a> confirmed him as king but cost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> its European possessions at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-utrecht">Utrecht</a> in 1713, while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nueva-planta-decrees">Nueva Planta decrees</a> abolished the separate institutions of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/crown-of-aragon">Crown of Aragon</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbons</a> built a more centralised state on the French model, with intendants, new academies and royal factories. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iii-of-spain">Charles III</a> (1759-1788) promoted roads, trade reform and enlightened ministers and expelled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a>. The monarchy was shattered by the 1808 French invasion; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-vii-of-spain">Ferdinand VII</a> then restored absolutism, and the American colonies won independence in the 1810s and 1820s.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isabella-ii-of-spain">Isabella II</a>'s reign was dominated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlist-wars">Carlist Wars</a>, generals and court scandal. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glorious-revolution-spain">Glorious Revolution</a> of September 1868 drove her into exile, opening the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sexenio-democratico">Sexenio Democrático</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/bourbon-spain.jpg" alt="Bourbon Spain" width="320" height="214"><figcaption>Image: Durero · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Spain_(1701%E2%80%931760).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1700 CE – 1868 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Madrid</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Philip V, Charles III, Isabella II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Spain (Bourbon), Monarchy of Spain</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1784&amp;focus=bourbon-spain" aria-label="Bourbon Spain on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4589 733 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Bourbon Spain lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4909 989L4794 911M4909 989L4979 949M4909 989L4984 945M4909 989L4991 1020M4909 989L5065 1017M4909 989L5053 958M4909 989L4885 950M4909 989L4909 989M4909 989L4910 989M4909 989L4909 989M4909 989L4909 989M4909 989L2659 1339M4909 989L2886 1342M4909 989L2738 1324"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4794 911h0M4979 949h0M4984 945h0M4991 1020h0M5065 1017h0M5053 958h0M4885 950h0M4909 989h0M4910 989h0M4909 989h0M4909 989h0M2659 1339h0M2886 1342h0M2738 1324h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4909 989h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4909 989h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Madrid. <a href="/atlas?year=1784&amp;focus=bourbon-spain">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
